  <p>
    The honest way to read this data: the world’s-largest-producer headline explains why India needs a
    dairy-technology workforce at all, but it is the organised sector’s roughly one-fifth-to-one-quarter
    share — and its steady growth — that actually explains why QA, procurement, plant-operations, and
    value-added R&D roles keep opening up. Total milk production and organised-sector hiring demand are
    two different numbers; do not let the first stand in for the second.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai-risk">Will automation change dairy-plant jobs</h2>

  <p>
    This is the question underneath every "is dairy science a good career" search once someone gets past
    the salary numbers. The honest answer is not a flat yes or no — it depends on which half of the job
    you actually do.
  </p>

